---
import Term from "../Term.astro";
import "./sternzeit.css";
---

<figure class="moon-figure" id="moon-view">
    <div class="moon-view" data-export="moon">
        <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-field="lockMoon" aria-pressed="true" title="Lock the view to the Moon itself: north up, no horizon">moon frame</button>
        <div class="moon-panel">
            <svg viewBox="-100 -100 200 200" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
            <button type="button" class="view-toggle libration-toggle" data-field="opticalLibration" aria-pressed="true" title="The tilt of the Moon's axis against its orbit and its uneven speed along it let us see a little around its edges">optical libration</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    {/* The lunation the moment is in, from one full moon to the next; its true phases are marked by the script. */}
    <label class="figure-slider" title="The lunation, full moon to full moon: drag, or turn the mouse wheel for an hour a notch">
        <span class="note">Lunation</span>
        <span class="figure-slider-rail">
            <input type="range" data-field="lunation" min="0" max="708" step="1" aria-label="Hours since the full moon" />
            <span class="figure-slider-scale" data-field="phases" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </span>
        <output data-field="lunationValue" title="Days since the full moon"></output>
    </label>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        The Moon as seen from the chosen place, its north pole (N) up: lit by the Sun, its night side in{" "}
        <Term of="Earthshine">earthshine</Term> (bluer when stronger). The arrow points to the Sun, as the normal at the
        point beneath it while that faces us, and from around the disc once it has turned away. The grid is the Moon's own, its center shifted by
        the <Term of="Libration">libration</Term>. The dashed
        circles are its size at apogee and perigee. Magnified, disc and horizon true to each other. Unlocked from the
        moon frame, the zenith is up (dashed) and the north pole turns against it by the{" "}
        <Term of="Position angle of axis">position angle of the axis</Term> and the{" "}
        <Term of="Parallactic angle">parallactic angle</Term> (arc). The slider runs through the lunation from full moon
        to full moon, an hour a step, its marks the true phases.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./moonview";
</script>
